  "description": "The mathematical language of computer science: propositional and predicate logic, sets, relations, functions, proof, induction, counting, recurrences, graphs and Boolean reasoning.",
  "prerequisites": [],
  "outcomes": [
    "Translate informal statements into propositional and predicate logic.",
    "Construct correct direct, contrapositive, contradiction and induction proofs.",
    "Reason about sets, relations, functions and finite structures.",
    "Solve foundational counting and recurrence problems.",
    "Use graph and Boolean models that later support algorithms, circuits and formal reasoning."
